---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import { release, observationsFor, url } from '../../lib/publication';
export function getStaticPaths() { return release.geographies.filter(g => ['state','union_territory','ut'].includes(g.type)).map(g => ({params:{slug:g.slug},props:{geography:g}})); }
const { geography } = Astro.props;
const rows = observationsFor(geography.id);
const isState = geography.type === 'state';
const karnatakaOrder = geography.id === 'india:karnataka' ? release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922') : undefined;
---
<Site title={`${geography.name} | evidence coverage`}><PageHeader title={geography.name} eyebrow={`${isState ? 'State' : 'Union territory'} · evidence record`} description="A local briefing begins with a precise place and a dated measurement. This release has a reviewed name record; local water indicators are listed below only if they pass the evidence checks." crumbs={[{label:'States & UTs',href:'/states/'},{label:geography.name}]} />
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="atlas-coverage"><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Administrative identity</p><strong>{isState ? 'State' : 'UT'}</strong><p>Listed by the National Portal of India; <a href={url('/sources/E-INDIA-ROSTER-20260923/')}>source record ↗</a></p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed local observations</p><strong>{rows.length}</strong><p>{rows.length ? 'Each row below includes its own source and period.' : 'No state-level measurement is approved in this snapshot.'}</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Code & geometry</p><strong>—</strong><p>Official LGD code and reusable boundary have not been verified here.</p></div></div>{rows.length ? <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><caption>Reviewed measurements for {geography.name}</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Indicator</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Period</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(o => <tr><td>{o.metricId.replaceAll('_',' ')}</td><td>{o.value} {o.unit}</td><td>{o.periodStart.slice(0,10)} to {o.periodEnd.slice(0,10)}</td><td><a href={url(`/sources/${o.sourceId}/`)}>Source record ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div> : <div class="note"><strong>Local conditions are not measured on this page.</strong><p>Unknown is neither a zero nor proof of normal conditions. The national and four broad IMD region values cannot be assigned to {geography.name}.</p></div>}</div></section>
{karnatakaOrder && <section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Government action · separate from water measurements</p><h2>A dated drought declaration</h2><p>The order covers listed taluks, not every place in Karnataka. It authorizes relief action and directs a survey; this page has no approved finding that relief was delivered or that crop loss or household shortage was measured.</p><ClaimBlock claim={karnatakaOrder} heading="Karnataka Revenue Department order · 22 September 2026" /><p><a href={url('/response/')}>See the action-stage ledger ↗</a></p></div></section>}
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A reporting route for {geography.name}</p><h2>What would make this useful locally?</h2></div><p>These are evidence requirements, not claims about current conditions.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>01 · Rainfall in the right area</h3><p>Use a source with a stated {isState ? 'state' : 'territory'} footprint, period, normal and station coverage. Compare the same season and baseline before drawing a trend.</p><a href={url('/sources/')}>Rainfall source catalogue ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>02 · Water actually available</h3><p>Match reservoir or groundwater measurements to their catchments and observation dates. Rainfall alone cannot establish household or farm supply.</p><a href={url('/basins/')}>Basin context ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>03 · Service and response</h3><p>Find dated utility notices, quality tests and action records. Separate announcement, funding, implementation and measured result.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>Response tracker method ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/explore/?view=coverage')}>Compare coverage ↗</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/journalists/')}>Reuse the evidence ↗</a></div><p class="small muted">Directory ID: {geography.id}. Roster snapshot version: {geography.version || 'not recorded'}. No map geometry is included for this record.</p></div></section></Site>
